*> IC101A -- "basic CALL statement" test from the NIST COBOL-85 suite.
*> The whole program is the CCVS85 test harness: it OPENs a PRINT-FILE,
*> runs five CALL "IC102A" USING DN1 tests, and WRITEs a pass/fail report.
*>
*> We drive one CALL test in isolation with `PERFORM ... THRU`, which bounds
*> reachability to that paragraph range so the harness's later CLOSE of the
*> (never-opened) PRINT-FILE is not reached. The subprogram IC102A is mocked
*> to return DN1 = 1 (its documented contract), which makes the test pass.
TESTSUITE "IC101A basic CALL statement tests"

TESTCASE "CALL-TEST-1 passes when IC102A returns DN1 = 1"
    MOCK CALL "IC102A"
        MOVE 1 TO DN1
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE DUMMY-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM CALL-TEST-1 THRU CALL-WRITE-1
    VERIFY CALL "IC102A" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY WRITE DUMMY-RECORD WAS PERFORMED AT LEAST ONCE
